# [Ansible role {{ role_name }}](#{{ role_name }})

Install and configure {{ role_name }}.

## [Example Playbook](#example-playbook)

This example is taken from [`molecule/default/converge.yml`](molecule/default/converge.yml). There is no CI yet: the scenario is run by hand against an Incus container, as described in [Testing](#testing).

```yaml
---
- name: Converge
  hosts: all
  become: true
  gather_facts: true

  roles:
    - role: steelcj.{{ role_name }}
```

The machine needs to be prepared. In testing this is done using [`molecule/default/prepare.yml`](molecule/default/prepare.yml):

```yaml
---
- name: Prepare
  hosts: all
  gather_facts: false
  tasks:
    - name: Install Python, python3-apt and sudo
      ansible.builtin.raw: >-
        (command -v sudo && python3 -c "import apt") >/dev/null 2>&1 ||
        (apt-get update -q && apt-get install -y -q python3 python3-apt sudo)
      changed_when: false
```

On real hosts, [robertdebock.bootstrap](https://github.com/robertdebock/ansible-role-bootstrap) does the same.

## [Role Variables](#role-variables)

The default values for the variables are set in [`defaults/main.yml`](defaults/main.yml):

```yaml
---
# defaults file for {{ role_name }}

# Packages to install. The distribution's package names are in vars/main.yml.
# Set this to install a different list.
{{ role_name }}_packages: "{{ '{{' }} _{{ role_name }}_packages_resolved {{ '}}' }}"

# The service to start and enable, or an empty string for none.
{{ role_name }}_service: ""

# Connections where the service is not started, such as Docker containers.
{{ role_name }}_skip_connections:
  - container
  - docker
  - community.docker.docker
```

## [Requirements](#requirements)

- ansible-core 2.15 or later. The role itself uses ansible-core modules only.
- For the Molecule scenario: Molecule, the `incus` client with permission to use it, and the `community.general` collection for the `community.general.incus` connection plugin, listed in [`molecule/default/requirements.yml`](molecule/default/requirements.yml).

## [Testing](#testing)

The Molecule scenario launches `images:debian/13` as an Incus system container on the machine running Molecule, converges the role over `incus exec`, runs it again to prove it is idempotent, verifies the result and deletes the container:

```sh
molecule test
```

The full procedure, from setting up a virtual environment to finding the cause of a failure, is in the [Molecule testing guide](en/docs/guides/manual-testing/molecule-incus-testing-v0.1.0.md).

